From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] exfat: limit directory read-ahead to one page

exfat_find() calls exfat_count_dir_entries() on the child directory of every
positive directory lookup, and exfat_dir_readahead() then queues a read of a
whole cluster. With the default 128 KiB cluster size on 512 B sectors that is
256 single-sector buffer-head reads per directory, even for an empty one.

On an RK3326 handheld (Cortex-A35, SD card, 135 empty system directories,
cold cache) stat() of all directories takes 11-14 s with the current code
and 0.8 s with read-ahead limited to a page (3 runs each, same module code
otherwise, built as an out-of-tree copy for the A/B comparison).

---
--- a/fs/exfat/dir.c
+++ b/fs/exfat/dir.c
@@ -635,15 +635,18 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
-#define EXFAT_MAX_RA_SIZE     (128*1024)
+/*
+ * Directory read-ahead is limited to one page. Reading a whole cluster
+ * (up to 128 KiB, i.e. 256 single-sector buffer heads on 512 B sectors) for
+ * every directory that is looked up makes a cold stat() of many directories
+ * very slow on SD cards, even when the directories are empty.
+ */
 static int exfat_dir_readahead(struct super_block *sb, sector_t sec)
 {
 	struct exfat_sb_info *sbi = EXFAT_SB(sb);
 	struct buffer_head *bh;
-	unsigned int max_ra_count = EXFAT_MAX_RA_SIZE >> sb->s_blocksize_bits;
 	unsigned int page_ra_count = PAGE_SIZE >> sb->s_blocksize_bits;
-	unsigned int adj_ra_count = max(sbi->sect_per_clus, page_ra_count);
-	unsigned int ra_count = min(adj_ra_count, max_ra_count);
+	unsigned int ra_count = page_ra_count;
 
 	/* Read-ahead is not required */
 	if (sbi->sect_per_clus == 1)
